{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nGerrit 3359 (the agentic verdict adapter, merged aed975de61c) received 5 non-blocking review findings that were not addressed before it landed:\n\n1. `_agentic_outcome` in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py` (~:376) builds a fresh `LLMOutcome` whose diagnostic is only `{\"exception_type\": ...}` for budget, tool-loop and truncation failures. That drops the run-shape `diagnostic` dict which `run_failure.interpret_failure` already attaches to `LLMBudgetExhaustedError` and `RunawayToolLoopError`, so an operator reading a failed agentic verdict loses the step and call counts.\n2. The comment above the pipeline-only post-dispatch tail in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` (~:624) still lists \"interim\" agentic verdicts, which no longer exist.\n3. No test checks that production `structured.check_stop_reason` sets `UnretryableOutputError.stop_reason`; the failure-class tests set it by hand.\n4. No test checks that a DET advisory finding and the agent call's `provider_provenance` reach the adapted agentic verdict through `gates/plan-review.yaml`.\n5. The truncation failure-class table covers `max_tokens` but not `length`.\n\n## Approach\n\n- In `_agentic_outcome`'s `fixed(...)` helper, build the diagnostic as `failure.sanitize_diagnostic({\"exception_type\": type(exc).__name__, **dict(getattr(exc, \"diagnostic\", {}) or {})})`. `sanitize_diagnostic` (`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:120`) is the existing allowlist + redactor every other outcome diagnostic goes through, so no unsanitized text reaches the verdict.\n- Rewrite the comment to name the current agentic verdict kinds: floor, adapted and degraded.\n- Add tests:\n  - in `tests/unit/test_structured.py`, `check_stop_reason(\"refusal\")` and a `check_response` whose `provider_details` carries a `\"refusal\"` key each raise `UnretryableOutputError` with `stop_reason` set (`\"refusal\"`);\n  - in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`:\n    - a plan whose Layer-1 floor yields an advisory (e.g. empty `file_impact` → P9) reviewed under `engine=\"agentic\"` carries that DET advisory in `advisory`, and the verdict's `provider_provenance` equals what the fake runner stamped;\n    - a `length` truncation classifies as `CHANGE_SETTINGS`;\n    - an `LLMBudgetExhaustedError` carrying `diagnostic={\"steps\": 61}` yields a verdict whose `coverage.diagnostic` includes `steps`.\n\nNo new config key, flag or env var; no change to any verdict string.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (comment only)\n- tests/unit/test_structured.py\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The 4 new tests above pass, and `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py` passes in full.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794521380924833001,"uuid":"28c440a1-7157-4cd2-84d0-a66c09291540"}